Everything is configured correctly. Here's a summary of what was set up:

**Directory: `/srv/shared`**
- **Owner:** `root:research`
- **Base permissions:** `2770` (rwxrws---) with setgid bit set
- The `+` in the listing confirms ACLs are active

**Current ACLs:**
| Entry | Permissions |
|---|---|
| `user::rwx` | Owner (root) full access |
| `user:alice:rwx` | Alice full access |
| `user:bob:rwx` | Bob full access |
| `group::rwx` | Owning group full access |
| `group:research:rwx` | Research group full access |
| `mask::rwx` | Mask allows all named entries |
| `other::---` | No access for others |

**Default ACLs (inherited by new files/subdirectories):**
| Entry | Permissions |
|---|---|
| `default:user::rwx` | Owner inherits rwx |
| `default:user:alice:rwx` | Alice inherits rwx |
| `default:user:bob:rwx` | Bob inherits rwx |
| `default:group::rwx` | Owning group inherits rwx |
| `default:group:research:rwx` | Research group inherits rwx |
| `default:mask::rwx` | Mask allows full inherited permissions |
| `default:other::---` | Others get no inherited permissions |

**How it works:**
- The **setgid bit** ensures new files/directories inherit the `research` group
- **Default ACLs** ensure any file or subdirectory created inside inherits the same ACL entries (alice:rwx, bob:rwx, research:rwx, other:---)
- The **mask** is set to `rwx` so it doesn't restrict the effective permissions of any named user or group entry
- **Others** have no permissions at any level, blocking unauthorized access

